      "message": "Having this at the end of the method makes the code difficult to understand and maintain. I can see why it is necessary - tearDown always calls cleanUp() if mEm is not null, and cleanUp() will only behave correctly if setUp has succeeded - but it would be better if the assumptions were all at the beginning.\n\nNot sure how to do better though. AFAIK assumeXyz() doesn\u0027t work in tearDown() - did you try this? If it doesn\u0027t work, then the simplest thing seems to be a \"mSkipTeardown\", \"mSkipTests\", or \"mRunTests\" boolean. Something like:\n\n\n    @Before\n    public void setUp() throws Exception {\n        mRunTests \u003d mTm.isTetheringSupported() \u0026\u0026 mEm !\u003d null;\n        assumeTrue(mRunTest);\n        ...\n\n    @After\n    public void tearDown() throws Exception {\n        if (!mRunTest) return;",
